 "envs": [],
 "excluded_from_certification": "the kernel-off comparison arm. certify.merge keys on (env, device, host, threads) with no slot for an arm, so a before/after pair from one host collides and one silently supersedes the other -- on a tie, by path order. Only the arm reflecting the current tree is a certification row.",
 "how_this_exclusion_works": "certify.merge reads d.get('envs', []), so an empty list contributes no runs and no tier. The rows are kept under 'envs_not_for_certification'. Structural, so it holds wherever the file sits and survives a pull that recreates it."
}